Ordered by priority. Lead with non-negotiable values. Lower-priority desires may be traded off in argument.
★ [acc-desires-026] (priority: 5/5)
  "Deploying AI to Run Society at Scale" — A Desire within accelerationist discourse that advocates for deploying advanced artificial intelligence to manage and optimize macro-scale societal, economic, and political structures.
Encompasses: AI-driven resource allocation, global problem-solving, and enhanced public administration.
  ARGUE: coherence with stated principles, precedent, tradeoff acknowledgment
  ATTACK VIA: coherence challenge, analogical breakdown, generalization failure
  PREMISES: "AI systems can be made sufficiently reliable and robust to manage macro-scale societal systems without catastrophic failures." — attackable; "Human-led institutions are demonstrably inferior to AI-driven systems in efficiency, equity, or outcomes at scale." — attackable
  VULNERABLE: The core case for AI-driven societal management rests on the empirical failures of human institutions — corruption, inefficiency, slow crisis response — meaning that a sufficiently capable and well-aligned AI could objectively outperform incumbents; dismissing this possibility out of hand privileges the status quo over measurable human welfare gains.
★ [acc-desires-001] (priority: 4/5)
  "AI-Powered Abundance and Global Problem-Solving" — A Desire that AI will resolve fundamental human problems -- scarcity, disease, inequality, existential risk -- creating post-scarcity conditions and serving as a benevolent force for civilization.
Encompasses: Post-scarcity economics, global crisis resolution, AI as moral technology, AI as the answer to every major human challenge.
  ARGUE: coherence with stated principles, precedent, tradeoff acknowledgment
  ATTACK VIA: coherence challenge, analogical breakdown, generalization failure
  PREMISES: "Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) or superintelligence is achievable." — attackable; "Advanced AI systems can be reliably aligned with complex human values and benevolent goals." — attackable
  VULNERABLE: The strongest counterargument is that even if AI achieves superintelligence, ensuring its alignment with complex human values and preventing unintended catastrophic outcomes remains an unsolved, potentially intractable, problem, making its benevolence far from guaranteed.
★ [acc-desires-009] (priority: 3/5)
  "Automate Society's Operating System" — A Desire within accelerationist discourse that envisions artificial intelligence serving as the foundational, automated infrastructure for macro-scale societal, economic, and political resource allocation. 
Encompasses: Algorithmic governance frameworks, automated supply chain management, and cybernetic state administration.
  ARGUE: coherence with stated principles, precedent, tradeoff acknowledgment
  ATTACK VIA: coherence challenge, analogical breakdown, generalization failure
